;; Written by Claude, 2026-10-14, for Phase 17 step 5
;; (doc/developer/vms-sdl-interfaces.md, part 1, proposals 5 and 6,
;; approved by the user); reviewed by the user,
;; 2026-10-14. Why this is right:
;; - VmsArguments has no code of its own beyond its three procedures and
;;   Word: its types' layouts are poc's ordinary ones, each field aligned
;;   to its size, which are VMS's (StringDescriptor 8 bytes, length at 0,
;;   class and type at 2 and 3, address at 4; ItemListEntry3 12 bytes;
;;   ItemListEntry2 and IOStatusBlock 8).
;; - Word turns a length or code of 0 to 65,535 into the word VMS reads:
;;   over 32,767 it subtracts 65,536 (SUBL2), and the word is the
;;   value's low one, SYSTEM.VAL's truncation (CVTWL -4(FP), R0).
;; - Describe counts up to the first 0X, LEN or 65,535, and stores the
;;   length (Word's), 14 and 1 as bytes, and the text's address; its
;;   descriptor is a VAR record parameter of an Oberon procedure, so its
;;   tag is at 8(AP) and text at 12(AP), with its length at 16(AP).
;; - SetItem stores LEN(buffer), the byte size of an ARRAY OF SYSTEM.BYTE
;;   (24(AP)), cut to 65,535, the code, and the two addresses, each
;;   element of list checked against its length (trap 2); EndList clears
;;   the entry.
